From 1aa4646df37adde46730b652a3bc8f1818622f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TWRP Builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:53:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] connectivity: turn STP-PSM sleep back on

With gPsEnable = 0 the consys never sleeps, BTIF stays in the ON state
and refuses every system suspend, so the tablet never deep-sleeps. The
"Wait for ACT" wakeup timeout that led to disabling it no longer
occurs: Wi-Fi off/on, BT on/off and repeated suspend/resume work, and
the tablet spends about 92% of screen-off time in suspend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/conn_soc/core/wmt_lib.c   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-3.18/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/conn_soc/core/wmt_lib.c b/kernel-3.18/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/conn_soc/core/wmt_lib.c
index 8b337db76..77eb5c61a 100644
--- a/kernel-3.18/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/conn_soc/core/wmt_lib.c
+++ b/kernel-3.18/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/conn_soc/core/wmt_lib.c
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ static const WMT_IC_PIN_STATE cmb_aif2pin_stat[] = {
 
 #if CFG_WMT_PS_SUPPORT
 static UINT32 gPsIdleTime = STP_PSM_IDLE_TIME_SLEEP;
-static UINT32 gPsEnable = 0;
+static UINT32 gPsEnable = 1;
 static PF_WMT_SDIO_PSOP sdio_own_ctrl;
 #endif
 
